# Debug dump of a live installation's file records — real uploaded filenames
# and upload paths from whichever deployment produced it. Never source.
/files.json

# ★★★ Release bakes. This directory holds DB dumps, source/image tarballs AND
#   copies of .env taken before a password rotation — i.e. BOW_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   and POSTGRES_PASSWORD in plaintext, plus ~12GB of binaries. It was NOT
#   ignored, so `git add .` before a push would have published the encryption
#   key that every stored credential is sealed with. Ignoring `.env` alone did
#   nothing for the copies of it kept in here.
_backups/

# Sales / positioning collateral. These decks and comparison docs were written
# for customer conversations, not for the product — nothing in the codebase
# references them (grep for the prefix returns zero hits outside git), so they
# ship no behaviour and only publish internal positioning to anyone who clones.
# The files stay on disk; they are just not part of the source tree.
CityAgent-Insights-*.pptx
CityAgent-Insights-*.docx

# Working build log and defect list. CLAUDE.md is a running account of this
# installation: it names the production hostname, the operator's personal
# and admin email addresses, the local checkout path, the unreleased roadmap,
# and which file the database password lives in. None of it is needed to build,
# run or upgrade the product — DOCKER.md and UPGRADE.md carry the operator
# instructions. Kept on disk, out of the source tree.
#
# ★CLAUDE-SESSIONS.md is the dated session log, split out of CLAUDE.md on
# 2026-08-02 (it was 86% of a 267KB file that gets loaded in full every
# session). It carries exactly the same sensitive detail, so it is ignored for
# exactly the same reasons — and because an untracked file here would trip the
# "STOP if git status prints anything" gate in the by-hand upgrade procedure.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE-SESSIONS.md
TEST-DEFECTS.md

# Screenshots taken while debugging against the live instance. They show real
# connector configuration forms, directory tenant names and report contents —
# evidence for a fix, not documentation of the product. The written loops in
# docs/feedback-loops/*.md stay: source comments cite them by path in ~30
# places, so deleting those would orphan the reasoning behind real code.
docs/feedback-loops/assets/
docs/screenshots/
docs/design/screenshots/
docs/design/session-events-samples/
frontend/media/pr/


*.pyc
# backend/alembic.ini is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is the only place `script_location` is set, so without it alembic cannot
# find its migrations and the container crash-loops on
#     FAILED: No 'script_location' key found in configuration.
# — an error that names neither git nor the missing file. The rule used to be
# here, presumably on the assumption the file holds a connection string. It
# does not: sqlalchemy.url is commented out and the real URL comes from
# BOW_DATABASE_URL. The file stayed tracked (tracking beats ignoring), so
# clones worked, but it could never be re-added once removed.
backend/app.db

# Sandbox session state (credentials, tokens, IDs)
backend/sandbox_state.json

# Claude Code local settings overrides
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/*

backend/sandbox_main.py
# configs/bow-config.dev.entra.yaml used to be ignored here and has now been
# deleted. It was an unused SSO template carrying upstream's own Entra tenant
# and client id, with `enabled: true`. Nothing loaded it — but the YAML is the
# FALLBACK when instance_settings is empty, which is the state of every fresh
# install, so an enabled provider block sitting in a config file can put a
# sign-in button for someone else's directory on a login page that nobody
# configured. SSO providers belong in the database, edited through
# Settings > Identity Provider. Do not re-add provider config here.


